  "id": "Compound::DB00909 - Gene::768",
  "verbalization": "Zonisamide appears to interact with Ca9 through a series of molecular and biochemical pathways, suggesting a potential role in modulating calcium-related processes. The evidence indicates that Zonisamide binds to Ca13 or Ca5b, which then participate in reversible hydration of carbon dioxide or carbonate dehydratase activity. These processes are ultimately linked to Ca9, implying that Zonisamide may influence calcium homeostasis or related metabolic functions. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Zonisamide could affect Ca9, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a direct or indirect relationship between Zonisamide and Ca9, mediated through calcium-binding proteins and their enzymatic activities.",
